WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.940 --> 00:00:03.520
It's been a long time since we came to Lordran.

00:00:04.340 --> 00:00:07.640
In the years since, we've fought millions of battles together.

00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:10.680
We've told stories of gods and men.

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:15.960
And most importantly, we know how it ends; not with fire, as Gwyn hoped,

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:18.740
nor with the abyss, as Gwyn feared.

00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:23.160
It ends with ash, a painted world and a Dark Soul.

00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:31.220
Man was born from the dark, a soul that is kindled, flickers, dwindles and dies in the shadow of his gods.

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:34.660
The human form is fragile and death comes quickly.

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:39.580
But the spirit is strong, and it clings to life like only a mortal can.

00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:44.000
So, in a way, Man was not designed to become Undead.

00:00:44.420 --> 00:00:46.680
Fear of death is what lets us live.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:50.920
Take that away, and humanity
becomes harder to hold onto.

00:00:51.220 --> 00:00:54.540
Without humanity, you could become
more Hollow than Man.

00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:58.760
Yet a Hollow who would die for something
has nothing to fear,

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:02.680
for death simply becomes a stepping stone to his goal.

00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:07.820
Five years ago, we told nine Undead stories.

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:14.600
One of the strongest man ever to make it to Anor Londo, who simply fell from its rafters.

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:18.020
Another of a sorcerer in pursuit of great knowledge,

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:21.080
who was undone by the secrets he found.

00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:24.400
For some treasures are not meant for men.

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:28.820
And besides, even if you find the most
powerful weapon in the world

00:01:29.620 --> 00:01:33.460
there's no reason to think you can save those you love.

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:37.400
Mankind will never escape the curse of the gods,

00:01:37.980 --> 00:01:40.040
so why not put your faith in them?

00:01:40.340 --> 00:01:45.060
Perhaps if we offer up our humanity, we may receive their love in return?

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:49.040
But no, there was never any hope of that, was there?

00:01:49.880 --> 00:01:53.800
These were the stories of fools who dared to believe in something greater.

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:59.360
Hoping against hope that their final acts could have changed fate.

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:03.340
[Oscar]: Regrettably, I have failed in my mission...

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:06.100
But perhaps you can keep the torch lit...

00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:08.600
There is an old saying in my family...

00:02:09.040 --> 00:02:11.100
'Thou who art undead, art chosen.'

00:02:11.420 --> 00:02:16.840
'In thine exodus from the Undead Asylum, maketh pilgrimage to the land of Ancient Lords.'

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:19.260
'When thou ringeth the Bell of Awakening,'

00:02:19.900 --> 00:02:22.460
'the fate of the Undead thou shalt know.'

00:02:24.380 --> 00:02:27.000
[VaatiVidya]: 'If you fall down seven times, stand up eight.'

00:02:27.560 --> 00:02:30.420
That was the cry of the Undead, all those years ago.

00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:33.800
And, for the most part, theirs were the stories we told.

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:37.840
But it's not just the Undead who have
stories worth telling.

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:42.560
For in the years since, we've learned more about their Lords than ever before.

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:46.100
There are five stories I want to bring to you.

00:02:46.780 --> 00:02:51.560
The first is the tale of a chaotic civilization
doomed to fade.

00:02:52.820 --> 00:02:57.460
Another of a lonely Lord, who lost his domain of death to gods and men.

00:02:58.380 --> 00:03:02.860
And I could think of at least one who would have preferred death to the alternative.

00:03:03.880 --> 00:03:07.560
There's the story of a soul that
persisted throughout the ages.

00:03:08.460 --> 00:03:12.540
And, of course, the tale of the fearful God
that started it all.

00:03:13.660 --> 00:03:17.240
These are the stories that enthralled millions
of us for years,

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:21.480
and it's a privilege to bring them to you one last time.

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:24.200
Prepare to Cry.

